# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend / CLI — .env.local (created by `npx convex dev`, gitignored)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=dev:<deployment-name>
# VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://<deployment-name>.convex.cloud   # public URL, safe in the browser
# CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY='dev:<deployment-name>|…'               # lets the CLI push without `convex login`

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backend secrets & settings — NOT in any file. Set them on the Convex deployment:
#
#   npx convex env set NAME value
#   npx convex env list
#
# They are read only by Convex functions (convex/lib/config.ts) and never
# reach the browser. Do not prefix anything with VITE_.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Dashboard access (Convex Auth, invite-only). Empty = nobody can sign in (fail closed).
#   ALLOWED_EMAILS=you@example.com,colleague@example.com
#   ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS=vyaparapp.in
# Convex Auth signing keys + site URL (set once; generated, never committed):
#   JWT_PRIVATE_KEY=…   JWKS=…   SITE_URL=http://localhost:5180
#
# Eligibility: assigned_agent matching this (case-insensitive regex) = "already assigned"
#   EXCLUDED_ASSIGNEE_PATTERN=technotask
#
# Default Vyapar Desktop download URL (a campaign can override it)
#   DESKTOP_DOWNLOAD_URL=
#
# Times WhatsApp API — sending (phase 4). The key goes in the raw Authorization header.
#   TIMES_API_URL=https://vyaparm2d.timespanel.in/wa/v2
#   TIMES_API_KEY=
# Receiving replies (phase 5) — how Times authenticates webhook calls, once documented:
#   TIMES_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
#
# NVIDIA / Nemotron (phase 7). Free endpoints are rate-limited — not unlimited.
#   NVIDIA_API_KEY=
#   NVIDIA_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
#   NVIDIA_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b
